---
#1736 review: the structural check compares a generic type's fields at its
applied arguments. Here the arguments match (`[Int]` on both sides) but the
fields don't (`note: String` here, `note: Int` in the consumer's `Wrapper`),
so the rejection comes from that field-level comparison, not from the
argument list. (The consumer can't redeclare `Envelope` itself:
`bynk.consumes.name_conflict`. Structural compatibility ignores record names,
so a differently named generic reaches the same comparison.)
---
context demo.vault

exports transparent { Envelope }

type Envelope[T] = { item: T, note: String }

service readBack {
  on call(e: Envelope[Int]) -> Effect[Int] {
    e.item
  }
}
